WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:00.200
[The D Dorm]

3
00:00.410 --> 00:04.800
♫Ho-hi, ho-hi, ho-hi, ho...♫

4
00:05.520 --> 00:07.960
- ♫Whoo!♫ - ♫Whoo!♫

5
00:08.320 --> 00:10.560
- ♫Give us your lime♫ - ♫For a lemon♫

6
00:10.560 --> 00:11.720
♫Those who have a daughter♫

7
00:11.720 --> 00:12.660
♫Let’s trade for a son-in-law♫

8
00:12.660 --> 00:14.660
♫Come now, this guard is your in-law♫

9
00:14.660 --> 00:16.580
- ♫Talala♫ - ♫Talala♫

10
00:16.580 --> 00:20.020
♫Ba dum pum, pum, pum♫

11
00:20.020 --> 00:22.150
♫When will you accept my love?♫

12
00:22.150 --> 00:23.780
- Ugh! - Whoa...

13
00:23.780 --> 00:24.720
What are you guys doing?

14
00:24.720 --> 00:26.040
You guys are so loud.

15
00:26.040 --> 00:27.080
You too, Handyman Daeng.

16
00:27.080 --> 00:28.770
Why don't you stop your brother?

17
00:28.890 --> 00:30.340
Why do I have to stop him?

18
00:30.550 --> 00:32.800
Since my brother is handsome...

19
00:32.800 --> 00:34.010
cute,

20
00:34.010 --> 00:35.350
kind-hearted,

21
00:35.530 --> 00:37.750
and his heart is yours alone.

22
00:37.750 --> 00:39.660
He has lots of love to give you.

23
00:39.660 --> 00:42.180
I think what he has are diseases.

24
00:42.400 --> 00:43.600
From diabetes to

25
00:43.600 --> 00:44.680
- blocked arteries - Don't listen to her.

26
00:44.680 --> 00:47.240
to high blood pressure!

27
00:47.240 --> 00:50.210
♫Ba dum pum, pum, pum...♫

28
00:50.210 --> 00:50.680
Hey!

29
00:51.760 --> 00:52.920
You're acting like you're annoyed,

30
00:52.920 --> 00:54.120
but you played along, huh?

31
00:54.410 --> 00:54.760
Oops...

32
00:54.920 --> 00:56.840
If you have that many diseases, why don't you see a doctor?

33
00:56.840 --> 00:57.900
I did, but...

34
00:57.900 --> 00:58.530
But?

35
00:58.530 --> 01:03.380
- ♫Long time no see, I missed you so much♫ - ♫So much♫

36
01:03.380 --> 01:04.150
Hey!

37
01:04.450 --> 01:05.349
Stop playing along with them.

38
01:05.349 --> 01:06.220
I'm glad that you're here.

39
01:06.220 --> 01:07.360
I want to ask you something.

40
01:07.360 --> 01:08.950
Have the tenants from rooms 202,

41
01:09.340 --> 01:10.150
204,

42
01:10.320 --> 01:11.180
308,

43
01:11.350 --> 01:12.100
and 407

44
01:12.420 --> 01:13.440
come back to their rooms?

45
01:13.640 --> 01:14.250
Oh,

46
01:14.700 --> 01:17.350
I think Mr. Duong from room 204

47
01:17.770 --> 01:19.450
- is in his room today. - That's right.

48
01:19.450 --> 01:20.240
He is?

49
01:20.240 --> 01:20.680
- Yes. - Yes.

50
01:20.680 --> 01:21.380
Hey,

51
01:21.380 --> 01:23.220
shall we go talk to him in room 204?

52
01:23.220 --> 01:23.850
Yeah, alright.

53
01:24.740 --> 01:25.460
Dobby,

54
01:26.120 --> 01:28.039
What outfit did you burn for me?!

55
01:28.039 --> 01:28.800
Huh?!

56
01:29.080 --> 01:30.180
I am not a turtle.

57
01:31.090 --> 01:31.750
Hey,

58
01:31.750 --> 01:33.300
is our dorm near a canal?

59
01:33.890 --> 01:36.000
I think I saw a turtle walking around here yesterday.

60
01:36.000 --> 01:36.550
Huh?!

61
01:38.330 --> 01:40.600
Our dorm isn't close to any canals, though.

62
01:40.600 --> 01:42.550
Then it might be one of the tenants' pets.

63
01:42.550 --> 01:44.220
Can you describe its appearance

64
01:44.220 --> 01:44.950
to me?

65
01:45.720 --> 01:47.920
This turtle...is so old!

66
01:48.550 --> 01:49.220
Old turtle...

67
01:49.220 --> 01:50.289
But he acts like a child.

68
01:50.810 --> 01:51.700
One more thing,

69
01:51.700 --> 01:53.479
he's a coward

70
01:53.920 --> 01:55.170
who likes to hide in his shell.

71
01:56.060 --> 01:57.320
And won't accept the truth.

72
01:57.320 --> 01:58.150
Hey,

73
01:58.400 --> 02:01.340
are you talking about an actual turtle? Or are you insulting someone?

74
02:01.600 --> 02:02.040
Right?

75
02:02.040 --> 02:03.320
Of course I'm talking about a turtle.

76
02:03.850 --> 02:04.820
Who else would I insult?

77
02:05.200 --> 02:05.970
Why?

78
02:06.440 --> 02:07.750
Is there anyone who looks like a turtle around here?

79
02:08.650 --> 02:09.530
I see.

80
02:09.530 --> 02:10.320
There is no one else.

81
02:10.320 --> 02:10.960
You are talking about me.

82
02:12.040 --> 02:12.550
Dobby,

83
02:12.930 --> 02:14.170
what did I even do to you?

84
02:14.170 --> 02:14.560
Huh?

85
02:14.560 --> 02:15.500
Why are you insulting me?!

86
02:16.650 --> 02:18.980
Come on, let's go to room 204.

87
02:19.160 --> 02:19.750
Okay.

88
02:20.020 --> 02:21.570
Hey, answer me... Hey!

89
02:21.570 --> 02:23.600
♫Ho-hi...♫

90
02:23.600 --> 02:24.380
Dobby!

91
02:26.490 --> 02:27.450
You got rejected.

92
02:29.160 --> 02:36.970
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

93
02:38.990 --> 02:45.910
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

94
02:45.910 --> 02:51.810
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

95
02:53.320 --> 02:59.640
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

96
03:00.340 --> 03:04.910
♫One day, we'll find what we're yearning for♫

97
03:04.910 --> 03:08.560
♫Walking alone is fine, but it's better when you're by my side♫

98
03:08.560 --> 03:12.150
♫It won't be lonely when you're here to walk beside♫

99
03:12.150 --> 03:15.070
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

100
03:15.720 --> 03:17.910
♫Like a love that remains, remains at the dorm♫

101
03:17.930 --> 03:25.100
♫Meaningful love and good things await on every path♫

102
03:25.100 --> 03:32.300
♫It might not be a coincidence that we get to meet♫

103
03:32.300 --> 03:39.500
♫There might be hidden meanings on the path beneath our feet♫

104
03:39.500 --> 03:46.700
♫Perhaps the D Dorm is what led me to meet you♫

105
03:46.700 --> 03:50.490
[The D Dorm]

106
03:50.570 --> 03:51.370
Mm...

107
03:51.370 --> 03:52.460
I think this room has the potential.

108
03:53.460 --> 03:53.970
Ow!

109
03:54.000 --> 03:54.550
- Oh? - Whoa...

110
03:55.290 --> 03:55.750
Ouch...

111
03:56.320 --> 03:57.290
I'm sorry.

112
04:06.210 --> 04:09.080
[Duong, occupation: stock trader]

113
04:09.210 --> 04:10.660
Are you hurt?

114
04:10.800 --> 04:11.350
Oh?

115
04:11.890 --> 04:13.580
Are you Mr. Duong from room 204?

116
04:13.880 --> 04:14.950
Oh...right.

117
04:14.950 --> 04:15.610
What is it to you?

118
04:15.960 --> 04:16.600
Huh?

119
04:16.820 --> 04:17.880
Does it look like steamed or fried taro?

120
04:18.250 --> 04:18.769
Then...

121
04:19.170 --> 04:20.290
buy me fried taro.

122
04:20.290 --> 04:22.019
- Oh... - I see...

123
04:22.019 --> 04:23.540
- He's on the phone. - He is, isn't he?

124
04:25.010 --> 04:25.750
I'm sorry about earlier.

125
04:26.050 --> 04:27.450
You bumped into me, right?

126
04:27.450 --> 04:28.600
Give me 2,000 baht.

127
04:28.600 --> 04:29.200
Huh?!

128
04:29.200 --> 04:29.700
What?

129
04:29.880 --> 04:31.170
Why do I have to pay you?

130
04:31.170 --> 04:32.680
Well, you bumped into me. And it hurt.

131
04:32.810 --> 04:34.040
You also wasted my time.

132
04:34.150 --> 04:37.050
Most importantly, you made me look away from the stock charts.

133
04:37.050 --> 04:38.460
I could lose hundreds of thousands of baht

134
04:38.760 --> 04:40.460
in just a few seconds.

135
04:40.800 --> 04:41.350
Whoa...

136
04:41.700 --> 04:43.100
What? I'm not paying!

137
04:43.100 --> 04:44.810
Then work to repay me.

138
04:44.950 --> 04:45.960
Go put up these flyers.

139
04:46.490 --> 04:46.940
Huh?

140
04:46.940 --> 04:47.350
Hey...

141
04:47.780 --> 04:48.550
Hey,

142
04:49.010 --> 04:51.420
when you want someone to do something for you, ask nicely.

143
04:51.420 --> 04:53.010
Who would want to help if you talk like that?

144
04:53.200 --> 04:54.040
Yeah.

145
04:54.040 --> 04:55.960
If you can find my bird, I'll give you 5,000 baht.

146
04:55.960 --> 04:56.490
Ooh!

147
04:56.950 --> 04:58.150
Wow, even faster than me.

148
04:58.420 --> 04:59.560
I'll put them up all over our dorm.

149
04:59.760 --> 05:00.320
Hey,

150
05:00.690 --> 05:02.140
since you're here,

151
05:02.140 --> 05:04.890
do you happen to have a relative named Gaysorn?

152
05:04.890 --> 05:05.540
Missed gain.

153
05:05.540 --> 05:06.550
Huh?!

154
05:06.680 --> 05:08.100
Grandma Gaysorn sells grains?

155
05:08.100 --> 05:08.820
Buy the dip.

156
05:08.820 --> 05:10.650
So, does she sell grains or dips?

157
05:10.650 --> 05:11.610
Sell it to your father!

158
05:11.610 --> 05:12.360
Hey!

159
05:12.360 --> 05:13.640
- You're gonna get... - Whoa, whoa.

160
05:13.640 --> 05:14.780
Hey, calm down. What's wrong?

161
05:14.780 --> 05:16.720
- Wait, wait, wait. - He insulted us.

162
05:16.720 --> 05:17.780
He wasn't.

163
05:17.780 --> 05:18.810
He's on the phone.

164
05:19.120 --> 05:20.770
I told you to sell it to your father.

165
05:20.770 --> 05:22.490
- He likes that stock, doesn't he? - Oh.

166
05:22.490 --> 05:23.600
Grains...

167
05:24.240 --> 05:25.480
What a waste of my time.

168
05:25.480 --> 05:26.610
You're talking on the phone, right?

169
05:26.610 --> 05:27.780
I'm talking to you all.

170
05:27.780 --> 05:28.760
- Huh? - What?!

171
05:28.760 --> 05:29.200
What?

172
05:29.200 --> 05:31.160
How could you say that?!

173
05:32.040 --> 05:32.950
It seems like...

174
05:33.690 --> 05:35.800
he won't waste his time talking to us.

175
05:37.320 --> 05:38.280
Guard Dum, can I see that?

176
05:38.280 --> 05:38.950
What's this?

177
05:40.150 --> 05:42.860
"Missing Bird: Duidui.

178
05:42.860 --> 05:44.400
A reward of 5,000 baht.

179
05:44.580 --> 05:46.150
Find it, get paid."

180
05:46.620 --> 05:48.250
Dobby, how about this?

181
05:48.659 --> 05:50.810
You help him look for his bird

182
05:50.810 --> 05:52.460
to win him over.

183
05:52.460 --> 05:53.810
That way, he will talk to you.

184
05:54.340 --> 05:55.750
Everyone, how about this?

185
05:57.180 --> 05:58.810
We should all look for his bird.

186
05:59.240 --> 06:01.750
Because if we help him first, he might be willing to talk to us.

187
06:02.950 --> 06:04.900
See? My idea...

188
06:04.900 --> 06:05.890
Alright, everyone.

189
06:06.140 --> 06:07.010
What a great idea!

190
06:07.170 --> 06:08.220
We'll... Here.

191
06:08.410 --> 06:10.150
- Put it up here. - I... My idea...

192
06:10.530 --> 06:11.240
Dobby!

193
06:11.240 --> 06:11.930
It looks perfect here.

194
06:11.930 --> 06:13.620
Do I even exist or what? Huh?

195
06:13.620 --> 06:15.120
- Here, too. Alright, Guard Dum? - Dobby.

196
06:15.120 --> 06:16.150
- Here as well. - Yes, alright.

197
06:16.150 --> 06:16.980
Come on, follow me.

198
06:16.980 --> 06:18.590
- Come on. - Listen to me!

199
06:18.610 --> 06:20.210
[The D Dorm]

200
06:20.440 --> 06:22.020
What's this surprise supposed to be?

201
06:22.020 --> 06:23.480
I can't wait to see it.

202
06:23.480 --> 06:25.580
- Three, two, one! - Three, two, one!

203
06:25.580 --> 06:27.900
- Surprise! - Surprise!

204
06:27.900 --> 06:29.350
Whoa!

205
06:29.900 --> 06:32.760
Did you buy all of this for me? It's all brand-new?

206
06:32.950 --> 06:35.350
Ooh...

207
06:36.010 --> 06:37.120
Wow!

208
06:37.320 --> 06:38.260
Amazing.

209
06:38.260 --> 06:39.780
Where did you get the money from?

210
06:39.780 --> 06:41.120
I used the savings, Mom.

211
06:41.600 --> 06:43.750
Oh, how sweet of you...

212
06:45.810 --> 06:48.040
Aw...

213
06:48.040 --> 06:50.280
You didn't have to use the money you saved.

214
06:50.280 --> 06:51.640
It's alright, Mom.

215
06:51.640 --> 06:53.000
Cause the money we used

216
06:53.000 --> 06:54.060
came from your room.

217
06:54.890 --> 06:55.540
Here.

218
06:58.150 --> 06:59.220
Hey, Dollar.

219
06:59.220 --> 07:00.550
Are you a cop or a thief, huh?

220
07:00.960 --> 07:02.370
Hey, Mom...

221
07:02.370 --> 07:03.200
We're only borrowing.

222
07:03.200 --> 07:05.580
We'll pay you back after we get paid.

223
07:05.580 --> 07:07.180
Don't you think we should redecorate a little

224
07:07.180 --> 07:08.950
for our restaurant's grand reopening?

225
07:08.950 --> 07:09.690
That's right, Mom.

226
07:09.690 --> 07:11.220
Aw, it's okay.

227
07:16.150 --> 07:17.570
Yes, Pha?

228
07:18.410 --> 07:19.040
Oh.

229
07:19.220 --> 07:21.220
Alright, one moment.

230
07:21.720 --> 07:22.480
- Mom, - Hm?

231
07:22.480 --> 07:25.300
Pha called me to tell me that the cook on set is sick,

232
07:25.610 --> 07:27.160
so they asked if you could go instead?

233
07:27.160 --> 07:28.760
I can't. It's too sudden.

234
07:28.760 --> 07:30.010
Our shop isn't ready yet.

235
07:30.010 --> 07:31.080
- Dollar isn't free, either. - Mm.

236
07:31.080 --> 07:32.250
I can't do it alone.

237
07:32.250 --> 07:33.800
But they said they'll give us 15,000 baht.

238
07:33.800 --> 07:35.060
- Then what are we waiting for? - Whoa.

239
07:35.210 --> 07:37.010
Well, money talks, honey.

240
07:37.010 --> 07:38.400
Come on, Dollar!

241
07:38.400 --> 07:39.250
Carry the gas tank.

242
07:39.250 --> 07:40.000
Alright, Mom. Let's...

243
07:40.000 --> 07:41.100
Hello, Pha?

244
07:41.100 --> 07:42.810
- My mother... My family - Dollar!

245
07:42.810 --> 07:43.260
will go right away.

246
07:43.260 --> 07:44.770
- I'm not a gas tank. - Oh?

247
07:44.950 --> 07:45.960
- Mm. - Sorry, Mom.

248
07:45.960 --> 07:47.350
- Take our things to the car. - Okay, Pha.

249
07:47.460 --> 07:48.040
- Let's go. - Hurry, Mom.

250
07:48.040 --> 07:49.750
- Mom... - Let's go to the market first.

251
07:53.010 --> 07:53.530
Woo!

252
07:53.810 --> 07:54.800
What are you doing?!

253
07:55.080 --> 07:55.750
Woo!

254
07:57.300 --> 07:58.150
Duidui,

255
07:58.150 --> 07:59.020
where are you?

256
07:59.020 --> 08:00.340
Come out.

257
08:00.340 --> 08:02.440
We have sweet and delicious sunflower seeds for you.

258
08:02.440 --> 08:03.260
Come eat some.

259
08:03.770 --> 08:04.650
Come, Duidui.

260
08:05.210 --> 08:06.140
Ugh!

261
08:06.140 --> 08:07.690
What are you doing?

262
08:08.560 --> 08:09.980
Perhaps we're catching fish.

263
08:09.980 --> 08:10.780
- Oh. - Hm?

264
08:10.780 --> 08:12.200
We're all dressed up like this

265
08:12.200 --> 08:13.890
to look for a parrot.

266
08:13.890 --> 08:15.730
Hey, I'm giving it my all.

267
08:15.730 --> 08:16.760
I can only hope...

268
08:17.010 --> 08:18.820
that Gramps will find that 5,000 baht.

269
08:18.820 --> 08:19.440
Hm?

270
08:19.750 --> 08:20.400
What 5,000?

271
08:20.840 --> 08:23.180
Oh, I mean Grandma Gaysorn.

272
08:23.180 --> 08:24.260
The words sound alike.

273
08:24.550 --> 08:25.530
Not even close.

274
08:25.530 --> 08:27.720
Your outfits don't look like birds at all.

275
08:27.720 --> 08:29.350
More like you're performing a ritual dance.

276
08:29.350 --> 08:30.090
Hey!

277
08:30.090 --> 08:31.880
And the bird flew off a long time ago,

278
08:31.880 --> 08:33.370
so it won't be coming back around here.

279
08:33.370 --> 08:34.150
Hey, Ms. Danis,

280
08:34.419 --> 08:36.780
I saw the bird flying around here earlier.

281
08:37.039 --> 08:38.950
I tried to catch it, but I failed.

282
08:39.220 --> 08:39.730
Hey.

283
08:39.960 --> 08:41.770
But didn't you say you were going to see the director?

284
08:42.010 --> 08:42.809
Why are you here?

285
08:43.080 --> 08:44.450
I was going to.

286
08:44.450 --> 08:45.610
I thought I saw two crazy people,

287
08:46.660 --> 08:48.330
so I came here to help you out.

288
08:48.330 --> 08:50.360
I didn't think you'd be one of them, too.

289
08:51.090 --> 08:51.660
Is that so?

290
08:51.690 --> 08:52.640
- Yeah... - Oh, there you are, Duidui.

291
08:52.640 --> 08:54.000
- Duidui! - Duidui!

292
08:54.000 --> 08:54.550
Duidui!

293
08:54.550 --> 08:56.050
- Duidui, my foot! - Duidui...

294
08:56.380 --> 08:57.260
I'm leaving.

295
08:58.150 --> 08:59.970
We won't catch the bird because you're too loud.

296
08:59.970 --> 09:00.810
Ugh...

297
09:02.120 --> 09:02.610
What?

298
09:02.610 --> 09:03.360
Mr. Dobby.

299
09:03.860 --> 09:04.660
- Whoa. - That's...

300
09:04.850 --> 09:05.350
Is that...

301
09:05.720 --> 09:08.950
Maybe the parrot came down to eat the seeds?

302
09:09.530 --> 09:10.460
That means it worked.

303
09:10.460 --> 09:11.350
Come on.

304
09:12.210 --> 09:13.260
- Come on. - Get in there.

305
09:13.750 --> 09:14.810
Three...

306
09:21.220 --> 09:21.780
Got you.

307
09:24.310 --> 09:25.190
Hey!

308
09:26.010 --> 09:26.950
Oh, Mr. Dawin?

309
09:27.220 --> 09:28.150
What are you doing here?

310
09:28.150 --> 09:29.760
I was hiding to catch the bird,

311
09:30.420 --> 09:32.060
but I think I stepped on an ant nest.

312
09:32.060 --> 09:32.460
Ugh...

313
09:32.950 --> 09:34.150
You're short on money too, huh?

314
09:34.150 --> 09:35.770
I don't really care about that 5,000 baht.

315
09:36.250 --> 09:38.020
I only care about your five fingers.

316
09:38.020 --> 09:38.570
Give it to me.

317
09:38.570 --> 09:39.560
Whoa, whoa!

318
09:42.180 --> 09:43.750
I made a deal with Guard Dum.

319
09:44.040 --> 09:45.580
If I can catch the bird,

320
09:45.580 --> 09:46.780
he'll take the money.

321
09:47.140 --> 09:48.550
And I get to hold your hand.

322
09:48.980 --> 09:50.360
He can't worm his way out of this one

323
09:50.500 --> 09:53.210
because we made a contract!

324
09:53.780 --> 09:54.550
He's cautious.

325
09:56.060 --> 09:57.420
How dare you sell

326
09:57.780 --> 09:59.640
your beloved brother out like this?!

327
10:00.140 --> 10:00.760
Hey!

328
10:01.080 --> 10:02.400
Help me find Duidui first.

329
10:02.660 --> 10:03.760
You can deal with him later.

330
10:04.150 --> 10:06.550
Is this the parrot you're looking for?

331
10:08.180 --> 10:08.950
- Huh? - Huh?

332
10:09.140 --> 10:10.150
- Duidui! - Duidui!

333
10:10.380 --> 10:11.960
I was lifting this barbell,

334
10:11.960 --> 10:13.120
and it landed on my shoulder.

335
10:13.400 --> 10:14.570
Can someone come take it away?

336
10:14.810 --> 10:16.480
The weight is unbalanced. My muscles might end up uneven.

337
10:18.220 --> 10:18.780
Go, go, go.

338
10:19.210 --> 10:19.640
Hurry.

339
10:19.640 --> 10:20.780
Don't move around too much.

340
10:22.890 --> 10:23.610
Don't move.

341
10:23.890 --> 10:24.550
Stay still.

342
10:27.650 --> 10:28.410
Dolly,

343
10:28.640 --> 10:31.040
have you finished making the fried minced pork balls?

344
10:31.040 --> 10:32.040
Yes...

345
10:32.040 --> 10:33.060
Are you done?

346
10:33.060 --> 10:34.150
Anyway...

347
10:34.420 --> 10:35.610
take care, alright?

348
10:36.000 --> 10:37.380
If you want to eat something, just tell me.

349
10:37.530 --> 10:39.490
I'll ask Mom to make it for you.

350
10:40.300 --> 10:42.200
I hope your legs get better soon.

351
10:43.640 --> 10:44.950
I'll hang up now, Mr. Drip.

352
10:45.210 --> 10:46.600
I have to get back to work.

353
10:47.640 --> 10:48.550
Dolly!

354
10:49.000 --> 10:49.750
Oh?

355
10:50.050 --> 10:50.650
What is it?

356
10:50.650 --> 10:52.760
I said, have you finished making the pork?

357
10:54.250 --> 10:55.120
Look.

358
10:55.120 --> 10:57.320
I've been making them since this morning.

359
10:58.320 --> 10:59.350
Whoa!

360
10:59.900 --> 11:00.770
Heart-shaped?

361
11:00.940 --> 11:01.640
How creative.

362
11:01.640 --> 11:02.170
What?

363
11:02.170 --> 11:02.800
Hmph,

364
11:02.800 --> 11:03.800
how imaginative.

365
11:03.800 --> 11:05.240
You put in so much effort.

366
11:05.240 --> 11:06.550
Oh, Mom...

367
11:06.550 --> 11:08.570
we have to switch things up from time to time,

368
11:08.570 --> 11:10.020
so it won't be boring.

369
11:10.020 --> 11:11.040
That's enough.

370
11:11.040 --> 11:12.100
I'll do it myself.

371
11:12.100 --> 11:13.200
- Mom. - You're so slow.

372
11:13.370 --> 11:14.040
- Hey... - Oh?

373
11:14.420 --> 11:17.130
I told you to throw this bag of meatballs away this morning.

374
11:17.350 --> 11:18.550
It's already gone bad. Understand?

375
11:18.680 --> 11:19.250
Yes.

376
11:19.530 --> 11:20.080
Ugh...

377
11:20.080 --> 11:22.370
Stop wasting your time shaping these into hearts.

378
11:22.770 --> 11:25.290
The crew can eat meatballs in any shape just fine.

379
11:25.290 --> 11:26.950
- Roll it like this, then off it goes. - Okay.

380
11:27.770 --> 11:29.180
- Like this, see? - Mm.

381
11:29.350 --> 11:30.280
- Whoa! - Whoa!

382
11:30.280 --> 11:32.220
- Come here! - Whoa, whoa, what?

383
11:32.220 --> 11:34.150
I heard there's a lot of good food here.

384
11:34.300 --> 11:34.960
So why don't you...

385
11:34.960 --> 11:35.350
Serve!

386
11:35.490 --> 11:35.800
Serve!

387
11:35.800 --> 11:37.750
Serve me a dish?

388
11:42.040 --> 11:44.950
[Dim, occupation: extra]

389
11:45.680 --> 11:46.570
Hello, Granny.

390
11:47.600 --> 11:50.080
If you weren't so sweet-looking, I'd be angry.

391
11:50.300 --> 11:51.420
Oh, wait, wait, wait.

392
11:51.420 --> 11:52.410
- Calm down. - I'm sorry.

393
11:52.610 --> 11:54.550
Think of that as him practicing his lines before filming.

394
11:54.550 --> 11:56.210
Whoa...

395
11:56.210 --> 11:57.800
Stop being so aggressive for now.

396
11:57.940 --> 12:00.220
Don't lose focus so easily, understand?

397
12:00.220 --> 12:01.900
When you're acting off script,

398
12:01.900 --> 12:03.440
you have to stay in character.

399
12:03.440 --> 12:04.570
Stay in character.

400
12:04.570 --> 12:05.160
Understood?

401
12:05.520 --> 12:06.900
- Yes. - Good.

402
12:06.900 --> 12:09.100
I can't believe you can actually be this sensible.

403
12:09.940 --> 12:10.980
When he's at the dorm...

404
12:10.980 --> 12:11.350
Yeah?

405
12:11.460 --> 12:12.360
He's silly

406
12:12.520 --> 12:13.420
and goofy.

407
12:13.420 --> 12:15.560
Pa dum, dum. Pa ding, ding, ding.

408
12:15.560 --> 12:16.970
Doodle, doodle, doodle doo.

409
12:16.970 --> 12:19.240
Tootle ootle ootle, tootle ti toot...

410
12:19.240 --> 12:20.480
- Hey! - Whoa!

411
12:20.690 --> 12:22.150
You're not that different from him.

412
12:23.170 --> 12:23.780
Auntie,

413
12:23.780 --> 12:25.290
is there anything to eat? I'm so hungry.

414
12:25.290 --> 12:26.570
Oh, the rice hasn't even finished cooking.

415
12:26.570 --> 12:28.720
Where am I supposed to get energy from?!

416
12:31.000 --> 12:32.010
I'll snack on these for now.

417
12:32.290 --> 12:33.160
Don't!

418
12:33.160 --> 12:33.810
Ow.

419
12:33.810 --> 12:35.620
There won't be enough food to go with the rice.

420
12:36.360 --> 12:38.160
Dolly, Dodo has arrived on set.

421
12:38.340 --> 12:39.610
Come help him get dressed right away.

422
12:41.210 --> 12:42.040
Okay.

423
12:42.810 --> 12:44.620
Mom, Dodo's here. Hurry up, okay?

424
12:44.780 --> 12:46.940
Why didn't you turn on the stove?

425
12:47.140 --> 12:47.890
Can you turn up the heat?

426
12:48.160 --> 12:49.620
They're calling you. Go.

427
12:49.620 --> 12:51.140
Yes, I'm on my way.

428
12:52.620 --> 12:53.570
This will have to do.

429
12:53.770 --> 12:54.550
Auntie, I'll be taking this.

430
12:54.780 --> 12:56.220
I said no.

431
12:56.220 --> 12:57.600
The proportions are going to be off.

432
12:58.360 --> 12:59.710
What did he even take?

433
13:07.750 --> 13:08.820
Let's rehearse one more time.

434
13:08.820 --> 13:09.450
Okay.

435
13:09.640 --> 13:10.370
Action.

436
13:11.650 --> 13:14.400
This simple food isn't fit for Captain Salween!

437
13:14.400 --> 13:15.650
What ween? That's a river.

438
13:16.280 --> 13:16.860
Try again.

439
13:16.860 --> 13:17.800
Captain Sala Song!

440
13:17.800 --> 13:18.370
That's a temple!

441
13:19.770 --> 13:20.790
Captain Sinful!

442
13:20.950 --> 13:21.770
Ugh!

443
13:21.970 --> 13:23.120
It's Sarasin!

444
13:23.240 --> 13:24.550
The protagonist is "Sarasin."

445
13:24.690 --> 13:26.000
Try to focus.

446
13:26.280 --> 13:26.950
Are you alright?

447
13:27.450 --> 13:29.120
Well, I'm nervous...

448
13:29.120 --> 13:31.570
I have to act in a scene with my celebrity crush.

449
13:31.570 --> 13:33.440
I'm already too flustered.

450
13:33.580 --> 13:35.350
I'm squealing!

451
13:35.970 --> 13:36.890
I'll try to calm down.

452
13:36.890 --> 13:37.240
Mm.

453
13:37.420 --> 13:38.170
Okay...

454
13:58.570 --> 14:01.480
[Dodo, occupation: actor]

455
14:01.800 --> 14:02.810
Mr. Dodo...

456
14:04.440 --> 14:05.350
Can you let go now?

457
14:05.370 --> 14:06.010
Oops.

458
14:06.360 --> 14:07.210
I'm sorry.

459
14:07.520 --> 14:07.980
Come here.

460
14:08.800 --> 14:10.730
- Dodo, hello. - Hello.

461
14:10.730 --> 14:11.780
Are you alright?

462
14:11.890 --> 14:12.550
I'm fine.

463
14:12.740 --> 14:14.130
Have you started filming?

464
14:14.130 --> 14:15.810
Uh, while we were waiting for you,

465
14:15.810 --> 14:17.170
we filmed a few scenes.

466
14:17.170 --> 14:18.880
We'll finish those up,

467
14:18.880 --> 14:20.330
then we'll film yours, alright?

468
14:20.330 --> 14:21.930
Oh...so you're implying that

469
14:22.280 --> 14:23.800
I wasted your time?

470
14:23.800 --> 14:24.550
Oops.

471
14:24.810 --> 14:26.000
Then go ahead and replace the lead actor.

472
14:26.240 --> 14:27.610
Uh... Wait, wait, wait, Dodo.

473
14:27.610 --> 14:28.770
Calm down, okay?

474
14:28.770 --> 14:31.180
Who would dare say that to you?

475
14:31.180 --> 14:32.300
No need to change the lead actor.

476
14:32.300 --> 14:34.150
I'll change the schedule for you.

477
14:34.150 --> 14:35.350
Alright, stop everything

478
14:35.350 --> 14:36.220
and film Dodo's scenes first.

479
14:36.220 --> 14:37.060
Okay, tell the crew.

480
14:37.060 --> 14:38.400
Hey, stop everything. Come on.

481
14:39.320 --> 14:40.040
Director,

482
14:40.040 --> 14:41.530
- Yes? - when will we get to have lunch, then?

483
14:41.730 --> 14:42.360
Who is this?

484
14:42.940 --> 14:43.750
Oh...

485
14:44.100 --> 14:44.720
Who?

486
14:46.040 --> 14:47.140
I'm a supporting actor.

487
14:47.350 --> 14:48.100
Oh...

488
14:48.100 --> 14:50.120
He'll be supporting you in the scene.

489
14:50.120 --> 14:50.950
Hello.

490
14:51.690 --> 14:53.700
If he's hungry, let him eat.

491
14:54.550 --> 14:55.750
- Wow, thank you so much. - How kind.

492
14:55.750 --> 14:56.950
We'll find a replacement.

493
14:56.950 --> 14:57.620
I'm in a rush here.

494
14:57.800 --> 14:58.570
- Whoa. - Hey.

495
14:58.970 --> 14:59.540
Just hold out a little longer.

496
14:59.540 --> 15:00.380
- Dodo. - Yes.

497
15:00.540 --> 15:01.750
Dodo!

498
15:04.960 --> 15:06.930
That is your celebrity crush?

499
15:06.930 --> 15:08.130
That's a villain.

500
15:08.620 --> 15:11.040
How could I know he'd act like that?

501
15:11.160 --> 15:13.750
It's a good thing I ate some fermented pork balls earlier.

502
15:14.400 --> 15:14.950
Hm?

503
15:17.060 --> 15:17.780
Fermented pork?

504
15:17.900 --> 15:19.750
Well, it was sour, so I figured it was fermented pork.

505
15:23.700 --> 15:25.140
[The D Dorm]

506
15:25.140 --> 15:25.930
Mr. Duong,

507
15:25.930 --> 15:28.760
you can check if this is the bird you're looking for.

508
15:29.090 --> 15:31.020
We can talk about the reward later.

509
15:31.020 --> 15:31.900
Tell that to your mother.

510
15:33.060 --> 15:34.900
I already told you not to let her buy that stock.

511
15:35.020 --> 15:36.440
It's too risky.

512
15:36.550 --> 15:37.610
What did you say again?

513
15:37.890 --> 15:38.650
Oh,

514
15:38.650 --> 15:39.810
it's my mother's business.

515
15:40.420 --> 15:41.620
Anyway, let's go see the bird.

516
15:41.620 --> 15:43.080
Let's go, Mr. Duong.

517
15:43.080 --> 15:44.140
Here we are.

518
15:44.620 --> 15:45.400
Is this your bird?

519
15:46.400 --> 15:47.350
Duidui!

520
15:48.170 --> 15:49.320
My dear Duidui.

521
15:51.820 --> 15:52.420
Oh?

522
15:54.370 --> 15:55.750
Why is my bird so still?

523
15:58.890 --> 16:00.180
Who killed my bird?!

524
16:00.180 --> 16:00.780
Huh?!

525
16:07.600 --> 16:08.260
What?

526
16:08.950 --> 16:10.150
Why is it dead?

527
16:10.940 --> 16:11.690
Guard Dum?

528
16:11.880 --> 16:12.550
Handyman Daeng?

529
16:12.550 --> 16:13.490
What happened?!

530
16:16.360 --> 16:16.900
Hey,

531
16:16.900 --> 16:18.050
why are you all quiet?

532
16:19.100 --> 16:21.290
Day and I love this bird like our own child.

533
16:21.290 --> 16:22.880
Whoever did this, bring me 50,000 baht.

534
16:22.880 --> 16:23.780
Huh?!

535
16:25.750 --> 16:26.620
50,000?!

536
16:27.130 --> 16:28.700
Mr. Dobby killed your bird.

537
16:28.700 --> 16:29.350
Oh...

538
16:29.540 --> 16:30.170
Huh?!

539
16:30.960 --> 16:31.750
Mr. Dobby...

540
16:34.660 --> 16:35.570
I saw it with my own two eyes.

541
16:38.780 --> 16:39.930
♫Who wants to be rich?♫

542
16:39.930 --> 16:41.350
♫I do, I do♫

543
16:41.350 --> 16:42.550
♫Who wants five thousand baht?♫

544
16:42.550 --> 16:44.260
♫I do, I do♫

545
16:44.950 --> 16:46.480
How lucky.

546
16:46.480 --> 16:48.440
Let's feed Duidui.

547
16:48.440 --> 16:50.620
Shut the hell up, you foul-mouthed bird!

548
16:51.200 --> 16:52.420
Little Eggy.

549
16:52.600 --> 16:53.760
Little Eggy.

550
16:53.980 --> 16:55.140
Little Eggy.

551
16:55.330 --> 16:56.420
Little Eggy.

552
16:57.380 --> 16:59.540
Who taught you to call me that?

553
17:00.050 --> 17:00.550
Shut up!

554
17:00.690 --> 17:01.750
Little Eggy.

555
17:02.090 --> 17:03.170
Little Eggy.

556
17:03.290 --> 17:04.940
Do you have a death wish?

557
17:05.349 --> 17:05.819
Huh?

558
17:06.020 --> 17:07.130
You want this, right?

559
17:07.290 --> 17:08.450
Little Eggy.

560
17:08.730 --> 17:09.970
Little Eggy.

561
17:10.150 --> 17:11.349
Little Eggy.

562
17:12.060 --> 17:13.980
Shut the hell up, you foul-mouthed bird!

563
17:14.280 --> 17:14.950
Mm!

564
17:16.300 --> 17:17.349
Take this!

565
17:17.880 --> 17:19.260
I can't believe that...

566
17:19.940 --> 17:21.660
Just by saying...

567
17:21.660 --> 17:23.780
"Little Eggy, Little Eggy.

568
17:23.900 --> 17:24.960
Yours are even smaller than mine."

569
17:25.490 --> 17:26.770
It was just teasing you,

570
17:26.770 --> 17:27.660
but you

571
17:27.660 --> 17:28.150
were so...

572
17:28.530 --> 17:29.350
enraged.

573
17:29.350 --> 17:30.340
Your emotional breakdown

574
17:30.340 --> 17:32.020
drove you to spray insecticide

575
17:32.170 --> 17:35.210
on a cute little bird

576
17:35.210 --> 17:37.460
that was proof of their love.

577
17:37.460 --> 17:39.240
How could you do that?

578
17:39.240 --> 17:39.980
Ugh!

579
17:40.500 --> 17:41.350
You're getting carried away.

580
17:41.500 --> 17:42.410
What are you even saying?

581
17:42.410 --> 17:43.750
I didn't kill Duidui.

582
17:47.240 --> 17:48.200
Okay!

583
17:48.940 --> 17:49.970
I really was angry

584
17:50.220 --> 17:51.680
because Duidui kept saying,

585
17:51.900 --> 17:53.500
"Little Eggy, Little Eggy."

586
17:53.700 --> 17:54.760
What I was holding

587
17:55.520 --> 17:56.530
was ant killer spray.

588
17:56.690 --> 17:57.860
I lifted the cage

589
17:57.860 --> 17:59.570
to kill the ants underneath it

590
17:59.880 --> 18:01.450
so the bird wouldn't get bitten to death.

591
18:01.920 --> 18:02.950
I didn't kill it!

592
18:02.950 --> 18:05.090
You can say whatever you want,

593
18:05.850 --> 18:07.320
but my Duidui is dead.

594
18:07.600 --> 18:08.410
I don't care.

595
18:09.160 --> 18:10.600
Someone's gonna have to pay for this.

596
18:10.600 --> 18:11.520
I want 50,000 baht.

597
18:11.520 --> 18:12.280
Huh?!

598
18:13.140 --> 18:14.410
I'm not paying you 50,000

599
18:14.410 --> 18:15.570
because I didn't do it.

600
18:15.940 --> 18:18.780
But if there's someone who killed Duidui...

601
18:19.340 --> 18:19.930
Who?

602
18:20.320 --> 18:21.240
I think it has to be...

603
18:23.620 --> 18:24.550
Mr. Dollar.

604
18:26.680 --> 18:27.210
Hm?

605
18:27.820 --> 18:28.960
I'm talking about you. Don't turn around.

606
18:29.770 --> 18:30.550
Are you crazy?

607
18:30.680 --> 18:31.620
Why would I kill Duidui?

608
18:31.620 --> 18:32.520
Well, Duidui

609
18:33.340 --> 18:34.780
found out that

610
18:35.140 --> 18:36.550
you're a cop who accepted bribes.

611
18:36.810 --> 18:38.040
- Oh?! - Whoa?!

612
18:39.330 --> 18:39.770
Mm.

613
18:44.580 --> 18:45.240
Alright,

614
18:45.240 --> 18:47.350
we'll start this scene with...

615
18:47.480 --> 18:48.930
Captain Sarasin

616
18:48.930 --> 18:50.770
investigating a laab restaurant in disguise.

617
18:50.770 --> 18:53.060
When I give you the signal,

618
18:53.060 --> 18:56.330
Dodo will pick up some sticky rice with a chili.

619
18:56.570 --> 18:57.980
As you're about to eat,

620
18:58.500 --> 18:59.800
Kied and Yae will approach you.

621
18:59.800 --> 19:02.250
Then Yae will hold your hand

622
19:02.490 --> 19:05.170
and eat the sticky rice from your hand. After that...

623
19:05.350 --> 19:07.240
he'll tell you to get out of the subdistrict...

624
19:07.570 --> 19:08.060
Uh...

625
19:08.260 --> 19:10.150
Dodo, do you understand what I'm saying?

626
19:11.350 --> 19:12.050
I don't.

627
19:13.750 --> 19:14.840
I don't understand why you're asking.

628
19:15.780 --> 19:18.550
Why don't you worry about the extras who'll hold me back instead?

629
19:19.750 --> 19:20.950
I'm Dodo.

630
19:21.440 --> 19:23.060
I started acting when I was seven.

631
19:23.060 --> 19:23.720
Whoa...

632
19:24.040 --> 19:25.400
I studied acting for seven years.

633
19:25.400 --> 19:25.750
Whoa...

634
19:25.980 --> 19:27.320
The movies I acted in won awards...

635
19:33.220 --> 19:35.810
I was using a safety pin, but you never stood still.

636
19:36.010 --> 19:36.840
That's why you got pricked.

637
19:36.840 --> 19:38.200
Are you saying this is my fault?

638
19:38.320 --> 19:39.770
If you had brought me clothes that fit,

639
19:39.770 --> 19:41.350
you wouldn't have to fix them like this.

640
19:41.350 --> 19:42.940
Well, you got all muscular...

641
19:42.940 --> 19:43.620
Stop, stop, stop.

642
19:43.620 --> 19:45.490
Dolly, don't argue with him. Wrong means wrong,

643
19:45.490 --> 19:45.970
okay?

644
19:45.970 --> 19:46.450
Are you done?

645
19:46.450 --> 19:47.940
Are you done? Ready now? We'll continue filming.

646
19:47.940 --> 19:49.170
Get ready, get ready.

647
19:49.170 --> 19:49.600
Come, come.

648
19:49.600 --> 19:50.770
Get ready.

649
19:55.410 --> 19:57.650
'The Bullet Chilli.'

650
19:57.650 --> 19:59.350
Scene seven, Take one.

651
20:13.970 --> 20:15.290
These simple dishes

652
20:16.320 --> 20:18.010
won't be to your liking, Captain Sarasin.

653
20:24.320 --> 20:25.750
Didn't they say it wouldn't be spicy?

654
20:26.800 --> 20:28.150
This is so spicy.

655
20:30.000 --> 20:30.550
Hey!

656
20:31.610 --> 20:33.160
The headman said that...

657
20:33.700 --> 20:34.780
you have until tomorrow morning.

658
20:35.350 --> 20:38.500
By sunrise, you'd better be gone,

659
20:38.500 --> 20:39.960
Captain Sarasin.

660
20:41.850 --> 20:43.260
Then tell the Headman that...!

661
20:46.890 --> 20:48.290
Mom, have you put your phone on mute yet?

662
20:48.290 --> 20:49.290
Cut!

663
20:49.290 --> 20:50.580
Who forgot to put their phone on mute?

664
20:50.580 --> 20:51.450
Oh, uh...

665
20:52.150 --> 20:53.140
Who is it?

666
20:53.140 --> 20:54.550
Haven't you worked on a film set before?

667
20:54.550 --> 20:55.170
It's not mine.

668
20:55.170 --> 20:55.540
Hey!

669
20:55.540 --> 20:56.300
That's not my ringtone.

670
20:56.300 --> 20:57.800
- Who is it?! - My ringtone is 'Dance a little, black shirt.'

671
20:57.800 --> 20:58.720
How can you be this inconsiderate?

672
20:58.720 --> 21:00.300
Whose phone is it?!

673
21:00.410 --> 21:01.140
You...

674
21:02.120 --> 21:03.250
Uh, it's mine.

675
21:03.520 --> 21:04.800
I'll go take this call for a moment.

676
21:05.350 --> 21:06.160
- Hello? - No...

677
21:06.440 --> 21:07.810
No problem at all, Dodo.

678
21:07.830 --> 21:08.950
It's alright.

679
21:08.950 --> 21:09.800
Dodo...

680
21:13.220 --> 21:14.330
- Director? - Yes?

681
21:14.490 --> 21:15.810
Can I go to the toilet for a moment?

682
21:16.150 --> 21:17.800
Ugh, right now?

683
21:17.800 --> 21:19.610
Hold it in so we can continue filming

684
21:19.610 --> 21:20.260
when Dodo comes back.

685
21:20.580 --> 21:21.580
There he is.

686
21:21.580 --> 21:22.150
Uh...

687
21:22.490 --> 21:23.930
You've put it on silent mode now, right?

688
21:23.930 --> 21:24.920
Alright.

689
21:24.920 --> 21:25.540
Ready?

690
21:25.540 --> 21:26.950
Shall we continue? Let's do this.

691
21:27.290 --> 21:28.770
Everyone, let's continue!

692
21:33.280 --> 21:34.150
Put your phone on mute!

693
21:34.150 --> 21:34.770
I already did.

694
21:34.770 --> 21:35.560
That wasn't my ringtone.

695
21:35.560 --> 21:37.380
- 'The Bullet Chilli.' - My ringtone is 'Dance a little, black shirt.'

696
21:37.540 --> 21:39.360
- Okay. - Scene seven, Take two.

697
21:40.150 --> 21:41.010
Ready.

698
21:43.890 --> 21:45.160
These simple dishes

699
21:45.340 --> 21:47.140
won't be to your liking, Captain Sarasin.

700
21:53.240 --> 21:53.780
Hey!

701
21:54.810 --> 21:55.520
The headman...

702
21:57.310 --> 21:58.160
said...

703
21:59.350 --> 22:00.020
Cut!

704
22:00.980 --> 22:01.750
Cut.

705
22:01.750 --> 22:02.840
My scarf is crooked.

706
22:03.440 --> 22:04.440
Go check it for him.

707
22:04.660 --> 22:05.600
Ugh...

708
22:06.080 --> 22:06.870
Ooh...

709
22:09.620 --> 22:10.480
If there's anything

710
22:10.480 --> 22:11.610
crooked right now,

711
22:11.800 --> 22:12.980
it's my face.

712
22:13.600 --> 22:14.570
Hold it in, Dax.

713
22:15.340 --> 22:16.230
Hold it.

714
22:16.600 --> 22:17.160
Hold...

715
22:17.160 --> 22:18.440
It's so spicy, Dax.

716
22:23.350 --> 22:25.420
'The Bullet Chilli.'

717
22:25.420 --> 22:26.760
Scene seven, Take eight.

718
22:27.880 --> 22:28.780
Action!

719
22:41.800 --> 22:43.100
Then tell the headman that...!

720
22:43.410 --> 22:43.900
Cut!

721
22:43.900 --> 22:45.080
Cut, cut, cut!

722
22:45.080 --> 22:45.930
Dodo,

723
22:45.930 --> 22:46.580
uh...

724
22:46.930 --> 22:47.350
Uh...

725
22:47.900 --> 22:49.750
You skipped Kied's line.

726
22:50.090 --> 22:51.480
These two were too slow,

727
22:51.700 --> 22:52.730
and I was ready to act.

728
22:52.940 --> 22:53.770
You're right.

729
22:53.770 --> 22:55.330
Hey, you two will have to speed things up a bit,

730
22:55.490 --> 22:56.170
okay?

731
22:56.170 --> 22:57.170
- Yes... - Alright, alright, alright.

732
22:57.170 --> 22:58.150
Let's try again. Come on!

733
23:01.860 --> 23:02.800
Are you alright, Dax?

734
23:02.800 --> 23:03.580
Hold on a bit longer.

735
23:07.750 --> 23:08.640
Hey!

736
23:08.640 --> 23:10.020
I won't be able to do this if you keep breathing in my face.

737
23:10.580 --> 23:11.490
Stop it.

738
23:11.800 --> 23:13.160
Ugh, I can't hold it anymore. I really have to go.

739
23:13.420 --> 23:14.330
Director!

740
23:14.950 --> 23:15.620
What now?

741
23:15.890 --> 23:17.860
I can't take it anymore. Can I have a five-minute toilet break?

742
23:17.860 --> 23:18.550
Me, too.

743
23:18.550 --> 23:19.440
I would like to take a break.

744
23:19.440 --> 23:20.290
It's so spicy.

745
23:20.560 --> 23:21.760
- Alright, then... - So spicy.

746
23:21.760 --> 23:22.780
How can we take a break?

747
23:23.120 --> 23:24.740
I have to leave at 3 P.M.

748
23:25.140 --> 23:26.950
Are you guys even professionals?

749
23:26.950 --> 23:28.360
How can you hold up the shoot like this?

750
23:28.610 --> 23:30.140
Who even is the professional here?

751
23:30.560 --> 23:32.320
You're the one screwing this up.

752
23:32.320 --> 23:33.490
If they aren't ready,

753
23:34.150 --> 23:35.220
we can find replacements.

754
23:35.600 --> 23:36.290
- Ugh. - What?

755
23:36.290 --> 23:37.970
I'm in a rush, so don't waste my time.

756
23:37.970 --> 23:38.480
Uh...

757
23:39.250 --> 23:40.150
Hold on just a bit longer.

758
23:40.150 --> 23:41.020
It'll be over soon, yeah?

759
23:41.020 --> 23:42.050
You've got this,

760
23:42.550 --> 23:43.090
yes?

761
23:43.090 --> 23:43.750
- Alright. - Yes.

762
23:44.800 --> 23:45.770
Alright, everyone,

763
23:45.960 --> 23:46.610
one more time!

764
23:49.380 --> 23:50.600
Stop accusing me already.

765
23:50.950 --> 23:52.150
I never took any bribes.

766
23:52.640 --> 23:54.130
I can charge you with

767
23:54.360 --> 23:56.620
defaming an officer for making baseless accusations.

768
23:56.620 --> 23:57.780
This isn't baseless.

769
23:58.150 --> 23:59.450
I heard it with my own ears

770
23:59.600 --> 24:01.070
and saw it with my own two eyes!

771
24:03.420 --> 24:04.450
Yes, Mr. Duong,

772
24:05.160 --> 24:06.380
we found Duidui.

773
24:06.780 --> 24:08.540
The bird is in a cage in front of the office.

774
24:08.820 --> 24:10.530
It is safe and sound.

775
24:10.660 --> 24:13.200
You can come pick it up when you're free.

776
24:15.240 --> 24:15.970
Stop it.

777
24:16.580 --> 24:18.260
You could be charged under Section 136

778
24:18.550 --> 24:20.120
for insulting an officer.

779
24:20.950 --> 24:22.150
Dollar has been involved in bribery.

780
24:22.150 --> 24:22.490
Whoa...

781
24:22.490 --> 24:23.610
Dollar has been involved in bribery.

782
24:23.900 --> 24:24.680
Dollar has been involved in bribery.

783
24:24.700 --> 24:25.160
Dollar takes bribes...?

784
24:25.160 --> 24:26.130
I didn't!

785
24:26.680 --> 24:27.800
I said stop.

786
24:31.200 --> 24:31.900
Yes, Mom?

787
24:32.180 --> 24:33.220
Your hair straightener?

788
24:33.520 --> 24:34.800
Yeah. I'll go check it out for you.

789
24:34.800 --> 24:36.130
Dollar has been involved in bribery.

790
24:36.550 --> 24:37.750
Dollar has been involved in bribery.

791
24:37.880 --> 24:38.740
Dollar has been involved in bribery.

792
24:38.740 --> 24:39.370
Hey,

793
24:39.370 --> 24:40.150
stop it!

794
24:40.300 --> 24:42.550
If I come back downstairs and you're still saying that,

795
24:42.720 --> 24:43.750
I'm gonna break your neck!

796
24:47.700 --> 24:48.800
Maybe

797
24:48.800 --> 24:50.490
Duidui was killed to silence it

798
24:50.490 --> 24:52.540
after it learned that you are a cop who takes bribes.

799
24:52.540 --> 24:53.740
I can't believe that...

800
24:53.740 --> 24:55.750
the fatherly police officer...

801
24:55.750 --> 24:57.300
could be corrupt!

802
24:57.300 --> 24:57.800
Yeah.

803
24:58.150 --> 25:00.260
I usually see you as an aerobics instructor for old people.

804
25:00.660 --> 25:02.260
When did you even take bribes?

805
25:02.260 --> 25:03.290
What kind of bribe did you take?

806
25:03.560 --> 25:05.200
Did you give those old people

807
25:06.200 --> 25:07.390
the stretching chair?

808
25:07.430 --> 25:08.760
That's heinous.

809
25:08.760 --> 25:10.620
I don't care about that.

810
25:10.620 --> 25:11.880
Someone has to pay me

811
25:11.880 --> 25:13.020
50,000 baht!

812
25:13.930 --> 25:14.810
Ugh!

813
25:14.810 --> 25:15.800
Listen to me.

814
25:15.800 --> 25:17.350
I didn't kill the bird,

815
25:17.960 --> 25:19.450
and I never took any bribes.

816
25:19.600 --> 25:20.950
You want to know the truth, don't you?

817
25:21.170 --> 25:21.540
Mm.

818
25:21.690 --> 25:22.570
The truth is...

819
25:27.220 --> 25:29.060
I'm glad I went all in yesterday.

820
25:29.240 --> 25:30.550
My punches are far sharper now.

821
25:36.400 --> 25:38.040
Hello.

822
25:39.850 --> 25:41.170
You seem a bit thin.

823
25:41.760 --> 25:42.970
Want me to teach you bodybuilding?

824
25:43.360 --> 25:44.420
That way, you'll be muscular

825
25:44.420 --> 25:46.150
with beautiful muscles like me.

826
25:47.500 --> 25:48.550
Can you say,

827
25:49.640 --> 25:51.780
"Dollar has a great body"?

828
25:52.040 --> 25:53.350
Dollar has been involved in bribery.

829
25:53.720 --> 25:55.260
Very good...

830
25:55.440 --> 25:56.220
Hey!

831
25:56.810 --> 25:57.960
You can't say that.

832
25:58.660 --> 25:59.350
Try again.

833
25:59.850 --> 26:02.040
Dollar has a great body.

834
26:02.300 --> 26:03.660
Dollar has been involved in bribery.

835
26:03.860 --> 26:05.180
Dollar has been involved in bribery.

836
26:05.350 --> 26:06.440
Dollar has been involved in bribery.

837
26:06.440 --> 26:07.040
Stop.

838
26:07.040 --> 26:07.750
Stop it.

839
26:07.860 --> 26:08.980
Dollar has been involved in bribery.

840
26:09.060 --> 26:10.460
Dollar has been involved in bribery.

841
26:10.480 --> 26:11.090
Stop!

842
26:12.250 --> 26:14.280
- Oh. - Oh.

843
26:14.420 --> 26:16.570
- Dollar has a great body. - Dollar has a great body.

844
26:17.680 --> 26:18.890
Yes, "Dollar has a great body."

845
26:20.010 --> 26:21.290
That's what happened.

846
26:22.260 --> 26:23.350
I didn't kill Duidui.

847
26:25.010 --> 26:26.610
Then who did?

848
26:27.690 --> 26:28.520
Come to think of it...

849
26:28.740 --> 26:29.780
I'm suspicious of someone.

850
26:30.200 --> 26:31.750
He might be Duidui's killer.

851
26:32.220 --> 26:32.950
This person

852
26:33.460 --> 26:34.770
normally puts on

853
26:36.300 --> 26:38.200
a kind and caring front.

854
26:38.410 --> 26:38.950
Hm?

855
26:39.440 --> 26:39.970
Who?

856
26:41.090 --> 26:41.810
But today,

857
26:42.050 --> 26:43.750
I saw his cruel side.

858
26:45.250 --> 26:45.940
Handyman Daeng!

859
26:45.940 --> 26:46.960
Hm? Yes?

860
26:51.320 --> 26:52.040
Whoa?!

861
26:52.040 --> 26:52.800
It's not me.

862
26:53.350 --> 26:54.340
I didn't kill it!

863
26:59.530 --> 27:00.970
Do you feel better, Dim?

864
27:02.050 --> 27:02.580
Wow...

865
27:02.820 --> 27:03.970
What kind of film set

866
27:04.340 --> 27:05.760
doesn't prepare anything

867
27:05.760 --> 27:07.220
for a chili-eating scene?

868
27:07.570 --> 27:08.950
Not even a single carton of milk.

869
27:09.220 --> 27:10.150
Come on now.

870
27:10.300 --> 27:12.550
It's not entirely the crew's fault.

871
27:12.940 --> 27:16.150
They probably didn't think the lead actor would mess up

872
27:16.400 --> 27:17.660
such a simple scene,

873
27:18.100 --> 27:20.290
making someone eat almost 20 chili peppers.

874
27:20.660 --> 27:21.960
It's just the spice for me.

875
27:22.560 --> 27:23.490
But I don't know if Dax

876
27:23.490 --> 27:24.850
will have the energy to keep acting.

877
27:24.850 --> 27:25.410
Ooh...

878
27:25.410 --> 27:26.210
- I can do this. - Whoa...

879
27:26.210 --> 27:27.540
- Sit down. Sit, sit. - Oh...

880
27:27.970 --> 27:28.720
I'm alright.

881
27:28.720 --> 27:30.330
Would you like an electrolyte drink?

882
27:30.330 --> 27:31.750
No, no, don't.

883
27:32.420 --> 27:34.340
I wouldn't be able to keep it in my system anyway.

884
27:34.580 --> 27:35.100
Oh.

885
27:35.240 --> 27:35.930
Right now,

886
27:36.220 --> 27:37.420
I can't eat anything.

887
27:37.620 --> 27:38.820
Whatever I eat comes right out.

888
27:38.820 --> 27:39.400
Food goes in?

889
27:39.600 --> 27:40.150
It then comes out.

890
27:40.150 --> 27:41.350
- Oh. - Oh.

891
27:41.350 --> 27:42.210
You can do this.

892
27:42.210 --> 27:43.220
Alright, everyone.

893
27:43.220 --> 27:44.840
- Let's film the next scene. - They're calling you. Go.

894
27:44.840 --> 27:46.150
If you're ready, let's continue.

895
27:46.150 --> 27:46.970
Come, come.

896
27:47.000 --> 27:49.090
- I'll explain it to you. - You've got this.

897
27:49.750 --> 27:50.610
Ready?

898
27:50.610 --> 27:51.400
Uh...

899
27:51.660 --> 27:53.610
This scene will be...

900
27:53.610 --> 27:55.860
Captain Sarasin fights with Yae and Kied,

901
27:56.530 --> 27:56.950
okay?

902
27:56.950 --> 27:58.150
The fight will go like this...

903
27:58.150 --> 27:59.350
Dodo will fight with Dax.

904
27:59.600 --> 28:02.760
And Dodo will punch Dax to the ground.

905
28:02.950 --> 28:03.770
Then...

906
28:04.000 --> 28:04.940
Dim, right?

907
28:04.940 --> 28:06.300
Dim will join the scene...

908
28:06.300 --> 28:07.210
with this knife in his hand.

909
28:07.360 --> 28:08.760
Dim will approach Dodo from behind.

910
28:08.760 --> 28:10.150
But Dodo knows you're there,

911
28:10.150 --> 28:11.350
so he'll turn around and grab your wrist.

912
28:11.350 --> 28:12.550
Then you'll struggle back and forth,

913
28:12.720 --> 28:14.260
glaring at each other with hatred.

914
28:14.520 --> 28:15.560
That's the scene.

915
28:15.560 --> 28:16.150
Understood?

916
28:16.900 --> 28:17.770
- Okay. - Yes.

917
28:17.900 --> 28:19.120
Why are your lips so red?

918
28:19.120 --> 28:20.040
When did you put on more lipstick?

919
28:21.130 --> 28:23.210
You've done several scenes already. Why are you still nervous?

920
28:23.210 --> 28:23.880
Your lips look pale.

921
28:24.550 --> 28:25.040
Are you alright?

922
28:25.040 --> 28:26.020
- I'm alright. - You two can do this, right?

923
28:26.020 --> 28:26.560
You've got this.

924
28:26.560 --> 28:27.300
You can do this.

925
28:27.640 --> 28:28.150
Okay.

926
28:28.150 --> 28:29.350
- Okay. - Alright, go.

927
28:29.740 --> 28:30.240
Go.

928
28:30.240 --> 28:32.410
- Let's start. - Get into your positions.

929
28:32.770 --> 28:33.570
Action!

930
28:35.060 --> 28:35.560
Hey!

931
28:46.410 --> 28:47.540
Ow...

932
29:01.100 --> 29:02.200
It's spicy.

933
29:02.690 --> 29:03.640
Hold it in.

934
29:04.150 --> 29:05.560
It will end soon.

935
29:05.580 --> 29:06.780
Hold it...

936
29:09.700 --> 29:10.660
Hold...

937
29:11.620 --> 29:12.980
It will end soon.

938
29:14.770 --> 29:15.520
I can do this...

939
29:17.570 --> 29:19.290
I can't do this anymore!

940
29:44.950 --> 29:45.780
Oh!

941
29:46.160 --> 29:47.360
The Bullet Chilli

942
29:47.600 --> 29:49.420
is going to be The Bullet of Love at this point.

943
29:49.750 --> 29:50.250
Oh?

944
29:53.660 --> 29:54.250
Cut!

945
29:55.400 --> 29:57.140
What even was that acting?!

946
29:57.140 --> 29:59.580
You two have wasted my whole day.

947
30:00.400 --> 30:01.170
Director,

948
30:01.170 --> 30:01.940
replace them.

949
30:01.940 --> 30:02.950
I don't want to act with them anymore.

950
30:04.610 --> 30:05.800
Dodo!

951
30:09.930 --> 30:10.780
It's not me.

952
30:10.780 --> 30:11.350
That's not true.

953
30:11.800 --> 30:12.740
My brother is innocent.

954
30:13.320 --> 30:14.280
He's a good person.

955
30:14.450 --> 30:15.570
He couldn't have killed the bird.

956
30:16.000 --> 30:16.780
I'm defending him,

957
30:16.980 --> 30:18.810
no matter what you say.

958
30:21.100 --> 30:22.730
So you are accomplices, huh?

959
30:22.860 --> 30:24.370
Then you'll have to pay me 25,000 baht each.

960
30:24.370 --> 30:25.620
Oh, you bird murderer!

961
30:26.040 --> 30:27.130
How could you do this?

962
30:27.370 --> 30:28.150
You backstabber!

963
30:29.000 --> 30:30.170
I really didn't do it.

964
30:30.170 --> 30:31.080
But I saw it with my own eyes.

965
30:31.080 --> 30:31.580
Huh?

966
30:32.050 --> 30:34.970
You have the strongest motive here.

967
30:35.780 --> 30:36.300
Whoa...

968
30:36.300 --> 30:37.050
What?

969
30:37.330 --> 30:38.020
Oh...

970
30:41.570 --> 30:44.020
I checked and unplugged everything for you.

971
30:44.020 --> 30:45.580
Hey, Mom, don't hang up yet.

972
30:46.000 --> 30:47.140
When I was younger...

973
30:47.580 --> 30:48.800
how did you teach me to speak?

974
30:50.170 --> 30:52.370
What I do with that information is up to me, Mom.

975
30:52.900 --> 30:53.880
Ugh, no.

976
30:53.880 --> 30:54.900
I didn't get anyone pregnant.

977
30:54.900 --> 30:56.370
I don't have a child, Mom!

978
30:57.220 --> 30:58.150
I didn't... Ugh.

979
30:58.290 --> 30:59.100
I'm hanging up.

980
31:00.800 --> 31:02.810
I can't take this anymore!

981
31:03.690 --> 31:05.350
♫The monkey holds the tiger's paw♫

982
31:05.610 --> 31:06.740
♫The tiger holds the monkey's hand♫

983
31:06.740 --> 31:09.250
I said it's annoying! Shut up!

984
31:09.780 --> 31:11.080
♫The tiger holds the monkey's hand♫

985
31:12.040 --> 31:13.130
♫The monkey holds the tiger's paw♫

986
31:13.130 --> 31:14.950
If you don't stop,

987
31:14.950 --> 31:19.210
I'll strangle you to death!

988
31:20.640 --> 31:22.210
The birdcage is placed in front of your office.

989
31:22.410 --> 31:24.320
You couldn't stand the noise,

990
31:24.320 --> 31:25.380
so you got up

991
31:25.620 --> 31:27.800
and killed the bird out of spite.

992
31:29.730 --> 31:30.620
- Whoa... - Hey!

993
31:31.240 --> 31:32.240
It's not like that.

994
31:32.450 --> 31:34.650
- How cruel. - I really didn't kill Duidui.

995
31:34.850 --> 31:36.120
Did what I said

996
31:36.420 --> 31:37.500
actually happen, then?

997
31:37.750 --> 31:39.810
That...

998
31:42.550 --> 31:43.170
is true.

999
31:43.170 --> 31:44.340
- Oh? - Oh!

1000
31:45.330 --> 31:46.780
It might be true,

1001
31:48.100 --> 31:49.750
but Handyman Daeng didn't kill Duidui.

1002
31:50.870 --> 31:52.410
If you want me to back you up,

1003
31:52.860 --> 31:53.810
you know

1004
31:54.550 --> 31:55.750
what I expect in return.

1005
32:03.890 --> 32:04.660
Whoa...

1006
32:04.660 --> 32:05.170
Ugh.

1007
32:05.620 --> 32:06.290
What?

1008
32:07.090 --> 32:08.460
It's all because of you, you pervert.

1009
32:08.810 --> 32:10.680
You caused this misunderstanding.

1010
32:10.680 --> 32:11.570
What do you mean?

1011
32:12.550 --> 32:13.540
Who killed Duidui, then?

1012
32:13.960 --> 32:15.260
Nothing I said

1013
32:16.150 --> 32:17.350
was directed at Duidui,

1014
32:18.290 --> 32:18.810
but...

1015
32:19.380 --> 32:20.650
I was talking to Dawin!

1016
32:24.300 --> 32:27.980
I'll strangle you to death!

1017
32:27.980 --> 32:29.350
♫Never tired of holding hands♫

1018
32:29.350 --> 32:30.550
Please, Handyman Daeng,

1019
32:30.550 --> 32:31.750
let me hold your hand tonight.

1020
32:32.000 --> 32:33.200
I want to see ghosts.

1021
32:33.420 --> 32:34.380
Ugh,

1022
32:34.380 --> 32:36.200
you're so annoying.

1023
32:36.200 --> 32:37.060
I can't take this anymore.

1024
32:37.060 --> 32:38.170
Shut up already!

1025
32:38.170 --> 32:38.950
- Take this. - Ow.

1026
32:43.340 --> 32:43.750
Huh?

1027
32:43.750 --> 32:45.980
All of that commotion was you talking to Dawin...

1028
32:45.980 --> 32:46.900
and not the bird?

1029
32:47.610 --> 32:48.200
Yes.

1030
32:49.220 --> 32:49.960
Hey!

1031
32:50.370 --> 32:51.650
Will we even find out

1032
32:51.650 --> 32:53.090
who killed Duidui at this point?

1033
32:53.090 --> 32:54.930
You'll learn the truth

1034
32:55.750 --> 32:57.810
because I have evidence against the killer.

1035
33:00.010 --> 33:02.040
The murderer is in this video.

1036
33:03.380 --> 33:04.150
Good.

1037
33:04.780 --> 33:05.350
Come on,

1038
33:05.520 --> 33:06.290
let's find them.

1039
33:18.170 --> 33:20.050
Five thousand baht reward.

1040
33:20.340 --> 33:21.780
But the four of us found it at the same time.

1041
33:22.300 --> 33:24.360
How much will each of us get?

1042
33:24.360 --> 33:26.220
Four divided by one thousand...

1043
33:26.600 --> 33:27.320
No.

1044
33:27.680 --> 33:28.770
It'd be easier if I were the only one who found it.

1045
33:29.770 --> 33:31.400
You greedy chubby.

1046
33:31.750 --> 33:33.410
You greedy chubby.

1047
33:34.280 --> 33:35.760
You greedy chubby.

1048
33:36.010 --> 33:38.010
I've never been insulted by a bird before.

1049
33:38.720 --> 33:40.020
Keep it up, and you'll be my food.

1050
33:40.020 --> 33:40.620
Come here.

1051
33:40.620 --> 33:41.120
Hm?

1052
33:42.040 --> 33:42.550
Come here.

1053
33:44.950 --> 33:45.450
Oops!

1054
33:47.090 --> 33:47.780
Wow...

1055
33:48.020 --> 33:48.980
You pooped?

1056
33:51.610 --> 33:52.150
What?

1057
33:53.210 --> 33:54.770
Why are your legs sticking up like that?

1058
33:55.890 --> 33:56.620
Duidui?

1059
33:57.640 --> 33:58.410
Duidui?

1060
33:58.410 --> 33:59.120
Sleepy?

1061
34:00.890 --> 34:02.580
Whoa!

1062
34:05.170 --> 34:07.750
I want to poke you with my stick.

1063
34:09.520 --> 34:10.730
Duidui's killer...

1064
34:12.179 --> 34:13.090
is Guard Dum.

1065
34:17.620 --> 34:18.820
Mr. Dodo...

1066
34:19.400 --> 34:20.199
Mr. Dodo,

1067
34:20.199 --> 34:21.920
please don't replace us.

1068
34:21.920 --> 34:24.020
This is all my fault.

1069
34:24.020 --> 34:24.920
And...

1070
34:24.920 --> 34:25.929
I promise...

1071
34:25.929 --> 34:28.420
that I won't waste your time in the next scenes.

1072
34:31.050 --> 34:31.929
Please?

1073
34:32.179 --> 34:33.590
Yes, Mr. Dodo.

1074
34:33.929 --> 34:35.610
If you replace our extras,

1075
34:35.840 --> 34:38.000
we might not be able to use the costumes we have.

1076
34:38.000 --> 34:39.330
And that might be

1077
34:40.179 --> 34:41.800
a bigger waste of your time.

1078
34:43.080 --> 34:44.400
If you can't do it, just leave.

1079
34:46.150 --> 34:46.929
The sponsor

1080
34:46.929 --> 34:48.550
invested this much

1081
34:49.370 --> 34:50.760
because of me.

1082
34:52.040 --> 34:54.000
Do you know who's important here?

1083
34:54.690 --> 34:57.300
Do you think this movie could happen without me?

1084
34:58.760 --> 34:59.500
Will you,

1085
34:59.500 --> 35:00.080
you,

1086
35:00.290 --> 35:01.610
you, and you

1087
35:01.750 --> 35:02.950
have jobs?!

1088
35:08.600 --> 35:09.170
Hey.

1089
35:10.010 --> 35:11.560
Do you think you got this far

1090
35:12.000 --> 35:13.170
all on your own?

1091
35:15.570 --> 35:16.440
Yes!

1092
35:16.920 --> 35:18.660
It's all because of my looks.

1093
35:21.140 --> 35:23.000
You all have jobs

1094
35:23.790 --> 35:25.370
thanks to my good looks.

1095
35:27.570 --> 35:29.000
If we're talking about good looks,

1096
35:29.000 --> 35:30.260
I could also be the lead actor.

1097
35:31.490 --> 35:33.200
But I'm trying to prove to everyone

1098
35:33.660 --> 35:35.170
that I can play various roles.

1099
35:36.650 --> 35:37.910
And not rely solely on my looks,

1100
35:38.280 --> 35:39.440
which will fade as I age.

1101
35:40.900 --> 35:42.550
What a narcissistic speech.

1102
35:42.550 --> 35:43.210
But...

1103
35:43.210 --> 35:44.580
he said it in such a cool way.

1104
35:44.580 --> 35:45.330
Mm...

1105
35:48.280 --> 35:50.250
Do you think a movie only needs one lead actor?

1106
35:52.040 --> 35:53.170
The cameramen,

1107
35:53.690 --> 35:54.550
lighting team,

1108
35:55.000 --> 35:55.750
and prop team

1109
35:56.480 --> 35:58.750
are the ones who make beautiful cinematography possible.

1110
36:01.120 --> 36:02.100
There are extras

1111
36:03.260 --> 36:04.800
who liven up the movie.

1112
36:05.720 --> 36:06.760
You need makeup artists,

1113
36:07.580 --> 36:08.300
hair stylists,

1114
36:08.520 --> 36:09.320
the costume team,

1115
36:10.610 --> 36:11.770
and the cook.

1116
36:12.780 --> 36:14.950
If not for them, you wouldn't be standing right here!

1117
36:16.640 --> 36:18.210
Everyone is equally important,

1118
36:19.730 --> 36:21.870
so treat everyone as equals.

1119
36:37.750 --> 36:38.460
Dax,

1120
36:38.820 --> 36:39.420
that's enough.

1121
36:39.420 --> 36:40.800
We're all going to be fired.

1122
36:41.130 --> 36:41.800
Stop...

1123
36:41.800 --> 36:42.780
I agree...

1124
36:42.780 --> 36:44.460
with what Dax said, though.

1125
36:44.780 --> 36:45.570
Right, everyone?

1126
36:45.570 --> 36:46.620
- Yes! - Yes!

1127
36:46.620 --> 36:47.180
- Yes! - Dax!

1128
36:47.180 --> 36:48.550
- Dax! Dax! - Dax! Dax!

1129
36:48.700 --> 36:50.240
- Dax! - Dax!

1130
36:50.360 --> 36:51.340
- Dax! - Dax!

1131
36:51.340 --> 36:52.500
- Enough! - Dax!

1132
36:53.050 --> 36:53.810
Director,

1133
36:53.840 --> 36:54.880
fire the entire crew.

1134
36:55.450 --> 36:56.300
Are you serious?

1135
37:01.620 --> 37:03.200
You left me no choice.

1136
37:05.880 --> 37:06.800
What are you going to do?

1137
37:06.800 --> 37:08.130
Do you think posting this on social media...

1138
37:08.130 --> 37:09.730
will make them believe an insignificant extra like you?!

1139
37:17.880 --> 37:18.550
Hello?

1140
37:18.550 --> 37:19.650
Uh... Yes.

1141
37:19.750 --> 37:20.580
Pardon me?

1142
37:21.660 --> 37:22.150
Uh...

1143
37:23.020 --> 37:23.580
Okay.

1144
37:24.140 --> 37:24.960
I'll arrange that right away.

1145
37:27.940 --> 37:28.800
Look,

1146
37:29.210 --> 37:30.650
the higher-ups are going to take action.

1147
37:32.010 --> 37:33.800
Prepare to lose your jobs.

1148
37:33.890 --> 37:34.980
The person who is losing their job

1149
37:35.460 --> 37:36.480
is you!

1150
37:37.750 --> 37:38.680
You doofus.

1151
37:38.680 --> 37:39.490
- Oh! - Ooh!

1152
37:39.630 --> 37:42.080
The higher-ups told me to replace the lead actor.

1153
37:42.100 --> 37:42.760
Huh?!

1154
37:45.730 --> 37:47.220
If you do that, what will the sponsor think?

1155
37:47.220 --> 37:49.980
Our sponsor was the one who told me to replace you.

1156
37:50.970 --> 37:54.320
They don't want an ambassador who likes to put others down.

1157
37:54.320 --> 37:56.280
It tarnishes the brand's image!

1158
37:57.540 --> 37:59.090
And if you have any problems,

1159
37:59.330 --> 38:00.590
they said...

1160
38:00.980 --> 38:02.800
you can talk to the president's son.

1161
38:18.160 --> 38:18.980
Huh?

1162
38:18.980 --> 38:19.750
- Whoa. - Yes!

1163
38:21.140 --> 38:22.910
I'm the president's son.

1164
38:23.600 --> 38:24.550
The president's son?

1165
38:25.940 --> 38:27.540
I didn't want to do this,

1166
38:28.000 --> 38:30.400
but everyone here is equally important.

1167
38:30.400 --> 38:32.440
Someone like you

1168
38:32.440 --> 38:33.940
needs to be taught a lesson.

1169
38:34.510 --> 38:36.840
You were acting all high and mighty earlier,

1170
38:36.840 --> 38:38.950
but now you look like a kicked puppy.

1171
38:40.150 --> 38:41.800
Ooh, kicked puppy.

1172
38:41.800 --> 38:43.420
- Go, go, leave. - Kicked puppy.

1173
38:45.240 --> 38:46.450
Um, Director?

1174
38:46.770 --> 38:47.350
Who...

1175
38:47.720 --> 38:48.550
will be the lead actor now?

1176
38:48.900 --> 38:49.750
Lead actor, huh?

1177
38:50.950 --> 38:51.500
I wonder who.

1178
38:51.660 --> 38:52.530
- Huh? - Oh?

1179
38:52.890 --> 38:53.920
Or...

1180
38:53.920 --> 38:54.810
What about you, Dax?

1181
38:55.260 --> 38:56.320
I know I'm handsome.

1182
38:56.320 --> 38:56.690
Mm.

1183
38:56.690 --> 38:57.530
I know I'm cool.

1184
38:57.530 --> 38:58.150
Mm.

1185
38:58.150 --> 38:58.780
But I...

1186
38:59.130 --> 39:00.510
still aspire

1187
39:01.520 --> 39:03.320
to be the best extra there is!

1188
39:03.840 --> 39:04.780
- Ugh... - Huh?

1189
39:04.780 --> 39:05.770
He's a weird one,

1190
39:05.770 --> 39:06.920
turning down a lead role like that.

1191
39:06.920 --> 39:08.290
Yeah. What was he acting all cool for earlier?

1192
39:08.290 --> 39:08.820
Yeah.

1193
39:09.370 --> 39:10.150
What about me, Mom?

1194
39:10.290 --> 39:11.100
- Hm? - Oh.

1195
39:12.330 --> 39:13.540
- Hey, he's back. - What should we do?

1196
39:15.210 --> 39:16.150
Mr. Dim.

1197
39:20.370 --> 39:21.420
Mr. Dim...

1198
39:21.600 --> 39:22.570
Mr. Dim...

1199
39:22.850 --> 39:24.800
I'm so sorry, Mr. Dim.

1200
39:25.080 --> 39:27.500
Mr. Dim, if you fire me,

1201
39:27.520 --> 39:28.810
it will be a hassle for everyone.

1202
39:28.830 --> 39:30.610
It's also a waste of time.

1203
39:31.050 --> 39:32.950
Mr. Dim, please forgive me.

1204
39:33.220 --> 39:34.420
Mr. Dim, I promise

1205
39:34.420 --> 39:36.770
I won't act like this in front of you again.

1206
39:37.000 --> 39:39.130
Please let me continue being the lead actor,

1207
39:39.620 --> 39:40.780
Mr. Dim...

1208
39:41.610 --> 39:43.840
- Please... - Promise you'll behave?

1209
39:44.020 --> 39:44.800
Yes,

1210
39:44.800 --> 39:45.560
I promise.

1211
39:49.240 --> 39:50.450
You'll let me...

1212
39:50.450 --> 39:51.810
remain the lead actor, right?

1213
39:52.010 --> 39:52.760
Mr. Dim?

1214
39:53.350 --> 39:54.250
Mr. Dim?

1215
39:55.340 --> 39:56.460
Mr. Dim...

1216
39:56.820 --> 39:57.440
Hm?

1217
39:57.440 --> 39:58.500
You'll let me remain the lead actor, right?

1218
39:58.780 --> 39:59.760
What should I do?

1219
40:00.660 --> 40:01.570
Mr. Dim.

1220
40:01.570 --> 40:02.780
Mr. Dim, wait.

1221
40:02.780 --> 40:04.040
- Please let me be the lead actor. - I'll think about it.

1222
40:04.040 --> 40:05.020
Mr. Dim.

1223
40:05.620 --> 40:06.550
Mr. Dim, wait.

1224
40:06.820 --> 40:08.780
- Whoa... - Oh...

1225
40:08.950 --> 40:10.150
He completely changed, huh?

1226
40:10.320 --> 40:11.160
Mm.

1227
40:11.160 --> 40:12.900
Is he a chameleon or something?

1228
40:12.900 --> 40:13.790
Right?

1229
40:14.010 --> 40:15.120
I didn't do it!

1230
40:15.530 --> 40:17.740
Duidui died before I even touched it.

1231
40:17.930 --> 40:20.130
It might have died from shock

1232
40:20.420 --> 40:21.970
after seeing an Asian black bear standing nearby.

1233
40:22.290 --> 40:23.390
- Whoa... - Hey!

1234
40:24.330 --> 40:25.580
Stop badmouthing my brother!

1235
40:25.760 --> 40:27.630
He isn't an Asian black bear.

1236
40:27.900 --> 40:29.350
The most I'll allow is a bearcat.

1237
40:29.490 --> 40:30.440
Or maybe a sun bear.

1238
40:31.220 --> 40:32.160
Ooh, cute.

1239
40:32.160 --> 40:33.170
Ca-caw.

1240
40:33.170 --> 40:33.960
Stop it.

1241
40:35.460 --> 40:36.550
I can see that

1242
40:37.220 --> 40:39.170
Guard Dum really didn't do anything to the bird.

1243
40:40.650 --> 40:42.170
To keep things fair,

1244
40:42.890 --> 40:44.950
why don't we take it to the vet

1245
40:45.220 --> 40:46.150
to find out the cause of death?

1246
40:46.150 --> 40:47.700
- Yeah, yeah. - Great idea.

1247
40:47.700 --> 40:50.570
Are you trying to avoid paying me 50,000 baht?

1248
40:51.690 --> 40:52.970
What happened to Duidui?

1249
40:54.970 --> 40:57.880
[Day, occupation: veterinarian]

1250
40:58.560 --> 41:00.050
Here he is, the vet.

1251
41:00.310 --> 41:01.390
Day, it's him.

1252
41:01.690 --> 41:03.200
He killed our Duidui.

1253
41:03.200 --> 41:03.700
What?

1254
41:03.700 --> 41:05.170
He's refusing to take responsibility.

1255
41:05.650 --> 41:06.550
Duidui is dead?

1256
41:06.550 --> 41:07.280
Mm.

1257
41:07.580 --> 41:08.450
Duidui!

1258
41:08.720 --> 41:09.480
Duidui!

1259
41:09.840 --> 41:11.040
Peep, peep, peep.

1260
41:11.210 --> 41:13.100
Ook, ook, ook.

1261
41:13.260 --> 41:14.620
Peep, peep, peep.

1262
41:14.620 --> 41:16.680
Ook, ook, ook.

1263
41:17.810 --> 41:18.550
Hey...

1264
41:20.380 --> 41:22.400
Did anyone feed Duidui anything?

1265
41:23.160 --> 41:23.900
Uh...

1266
41:23.900 --> 41:24.920
Duidui had...

1267
41:24.920 --> 41:26.950
ooh-ah-ah.

1268
41:27.090 --> 41:29.090
Ook, ook, ook.

1269
41:29.090 --> 41:30.250
- Hey! - Ugh!

1270
41:30.550 --> 41:31.040
What the heck?

1271
41:31.040 --> 41:32.460
Allow me to answer.

1272
41:33.820 --> 41:36.250
Ever since we caught it, all we've given it

1273
41:36.550 --> 41:37.930
is the water in the tray.

1274
41:38.140 --> 41:40.450
You gave it dirty tap water, didn't you?

1275
41:41.810 --> 41:43.180
Pay me 50,000 baht.

1276
41:43.180 --> 41:44.000
Whoa...

1277
41:49.330 --> 41:50.530
Shut up, Duong.

1278
41:52.480 --> 41:54.420
You're acting like you care about Duidui

1279
41:54.420 --> 41:56.280
only because you want money from them, aren't you?

1280
41:56.730 --> 41:58.480
You didn't seem to care when Duidui was still alive.

1281
41:59.800 --> 42:00.550
What?

1282
42:00.550 --> 42:02.260
You're pretending that you care

1283
42:02.560 --> 42:04.150
just to get money from us?

1284
42:05.730 --> 42:07.750
If he actually takes good care of Duidui,

1285
42:07.980 --> 42:09.650
he won't let it starve.

1286
42:09.650 --> 42:11.060
He left it no choice but to fly out to find food,

1287
42:11.060 --> 42:12.930
and it ended up dying from diarrhea like this.

1288
42:12.930 --> 42:14.300
It died from diarrhea...

1289
42:14.480 --> 42:15.030
So,

1290
42:15.490 --> 42:16.660
the bird wasn't killed,

1291
42:16.900 --> 42:18.420
but it died from diarrhea?

1292
42:18.420 --> 42:19.020
Mm.

1293
42:19.360 --> 42:20.730
No wonder it pooped so much.

1294
42:20.730 --> 42:21.440
Hey, Day.

1295
42:22.010 --> 42:23.040
Can you stop being stupid?

1296
42:23.180 --> 42:24.800
Since the bird died,

1297
42:25.540 --> 42:27.210
we could've gotten some money from them.

1298
42:28.700 --> 42:29.650
Does this mean...

1299
42:30.420 --> 42:32.020
you're trying to steal from us?

1300
42:33.840 --> 42:35.350
Don't accuse me like that, Officer.

1301
42:35.350 --> 42:37.540
I'm just trying to protect his interests.

1302
42:38.880 --> 42:39.950
Is it really for me?

1303
42:40.150 --> 42:41.280
Or is it for yourself?

1304
42:41.660 --> 42:43.520
I went to find a new place to rent,

1305
42:43.520 --> 42:45.400
so I had to leave Duidui with you.

1306
42:45.850 --> 42:47.940
You even charged me for looking after it.

1307
42:48.170 --> 42:50.260
You were the one who caused its death,

1308
42:50.950 --> 42:52.320
so shouldn't you take responsibility?

1309
42:56.040 --> 42:57.480
Why am I the one responsible?

1310
42:58.150 --> 42:59.500
The bird is already dead,

1311
42:59.660 --> 43:01.050
and you've already moved away.

1312
43:01.330 --> 43:02.520
Isn't that the end of it?

1313
43:09.090 --> 43:09.760
Huh?

1314
43:10.200 --> 43:11.900
Your parents are buying stock in Tim's pot business?

1315
43:13.900 --> 43:15.130
Tell your parents this.

1316
43:15.130 --> 43:15.460
What?

1317
43:15.460 --> 43:16.560
They should stop trading stocks.

1318
43:18.550 --> 43:19.570
Look at what they pick...

1319
43:22.220 --> 43:23.250
Duidui...

1320
43:23.690 --> 43:24.890
I'm sorry for your loss, Mr. Day.

1321
43:25.210 --> 43:26.600
This is my fault.

1322
43:27.180 --> 43:29.010
I shouldn't have left Duidui with Duong.

1323
43:30.360 --> 43:31.520
I'm sorry, dear.

1324
43:32.380 --> 43:33.260
Duidui...

1325
43:33.900 --> 43:34.650
Oh, dear...

1326
43:34.650 --> 43:37.500
Peep, peep, peep.

1327
43:37.750 --> 43:38.740
Ook, ook, ook.

1328
43:38.950 --> 43:40.520
Ooh-ah-ah.

1329
43:40.520 --> 43:42.250
Ha-ha-ha.

1330
43:42.250 --> 43:43.100
Oh, no...

1331
43:43.100 --> 43:44.780
My poor Duidui...

1332
43:44.780 --> 43:45.860
Poor thing...

1333
43:46.480 --> 43:48.140
Is there a monkey in that cage?

1334
43:51.760 --> 43:53.130
I feel bad for him,

1335
43:53.690 --> 43:55.050
losing his bird like that.

1336
43:56.000 --> 43:57.580
He's probably very sad.

1337
43:59.570 --> 44:00.490
Yeah.

1338
44:00.720 --> 44:02.800
If I were him, I'd be heartbroken, too.

1339
44:08.010 --> 44:08.820
Ugh!

1340
44:08.820 --> 44:10.040
What's with you sneakily holding my hand?

1341
44:11.930 --> 44:13.220
Duidui, you poor thing.

1342
44:14.950 --> 44:15.810
You passed away...

1343
44:16.600 --> 44:17.960
without ever saying...

1344
44:18.700 --> 44:19.750
Dollar has a great body.

1345
44:20.040 --> 44:20.570
Ugh...

1346
44:20.770 --> 44:22.150
It probably had so much left unsaid.

1347
44:23.350 --> 44:24.550
Everyone in this dorm...

1348
44:24.740 --> 44:25.750
Dollar has a great body.

1349
44:27.400 --> 44:28.440
- Big muscles. - You got those big muscles

1350
44:28.440 --> 44:29.760
by injecting baking soda into them, right?

1351
44:30.730 --> 44:31.490
I didn't.

1352
44:36.850 --> 44:39.020
[The D Dorm]

1353
44:42.550 --> 44:43.750
Dobby,

1354
44:44.840 --> 44:46.150
his bird is already dead.

1355
44:46.320 --> 44:49.750
Why are you so sad about it?

1356
44:49.920 --> 44:52.800
I saw you sitting there looking glum for a while.

1357
44:54.690 --> 44:55.450
What?

1358
44:56.950 --> 45:00.000
Or is it that you want to learn how to speak like a bird?

1359
45:00.000 --> 45:02.060
I can teach you that.

1360
45:03.610 --> 45:04.800
Say...

1361
45:05.020 --> 45:07.750
Chu-cao, chu-cao, chu-cao.

1362
45:07.750 --> 45:09.100
Chu-cao, chu-cao.

1363
45:09.130 --> 45:10.530
Chu-cao, chu-cao, chu-cao.

1364
45:16.150 --> 45:16.760
Grandpa,

1365
45:18.550 --> 45:20.000
Duong thinks that...

1366
45:20.380 --> 45:22.150
now that the bird is dead, everything is over.

1367
45:22.530 --> 45:24.370
He doesn't have to take responsibility for it.

1368
45:24.760 --> 45:26.220
Do you think he's selfish?

1369
45:26.610 --> 45:28.150
He sure is selfish.

1370
45:30.320 --> 45:31.750
Don't you think you're being selfish as well?

1371
45:31.940 --> 45:32.760
Nonsense.

1372
45:33.530 --> 45:34.780
How am I selfish?

1373
45:35.050 --> 45:37.750
I heard everything you said to Uncle Tong on the rooftop.

1374
45:38.260 --> 45:40.300
I just want to take this secret

1375
45:40.300 --> 45:43.140
to my grave.

1376
45:44.200 --> 45:45.410
Tell me honestly, Grandpa.

1377
45:47.160 --> 45:48.550
Did you ever love my mother?

1378
45:49.180 --> 45:49.750
I did.

1379
45:49.880 --> 45:50.950
If you did,

1380
45:52.450 --> 45:55.340
why are you letting her carry all this guilt on her shoulders?

1381
45:55.900 --> 45:58.450
You think everything is over after you passed away, huh?

1382
45:59.090 --> 45:59.770
Did you know?

1383
46:00.340 --> 46:01.750
On the day you passed away,

1384
46:02.240 --> 46:03.800
Mom was crying.

1385
46:03.800 --> 46:05.960
She blamed herself, thinking it was her fault for leaving you behind.

1386
46:05.960 --> 46:08.080
When in fact, you were the one

1387
46:08.410 --> 46:10.370
who drove my mother away.

1388
46:15.500 --> 46:16.610
I did not know...

1389
46:18.570 --> 46:20.590
I thought she was happy.

1390
46:22.150 --> 46:23.350
I thought...

1391
46:25.290 --> 46:26.970
she had already forgotten about me...

1392
46:28.680 --> 46:30.200
I never knew...

1393
46:30.700 --> 46:32.170
Then carry that turtle shell

1394
46:33.120 --> 46:34.770
until you understand how my mother felt

1395
46:35.900 --> 46:37.260
carrying all that guilt.

1396
46:41.010 --> 46:42.100
Dobby...

1397
47:01.260 --> 47:02.070
I choose this card.

1398
47:02.150 --> 47:04.180
Be careful around high places these days.

1399
47:04.200 --> 47:05.580
It could be fatal!

1400
47:05.600 --> 47:07.370
Hey, Mom...

1401
47:07.580 --> 47:09.660
- Come on, go get changed. - I don't wanna be a muscle-obsessed

1402
47:09.680 --> 47:11.730
- gym rat like him. - Go get changed...

1403
47:11.770 --> 47:13.180
- Oh. - Whoa.

1404
47:13.400 --> 47:14.790
- Dolly! - Dolly!

1405
47:15.980 --> 47:16.550
Dolly!

1406
47:16.570 --> 47:18.410
Hello, everyone.

1407
47:18.430 --> 47:22.490
Today, I'm back at the D Dorm!

1408
47:22.510 --> 47:24.460
You're Grandma Gaysorn's relative?

1409
47:26.880 --> 47:28.290
Is Grandma Gaysorn...

1410
47:29.670 --> 47:30.690
still alive?

1411
47:33.590 --> 47:37.030
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1412
47:37.190 --> 47:40.970
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1413
47:43.450 --> 47:48.930
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

1414
47:50.680 --> 47:55.380
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

1415
47:57.860 --> 48:04.000
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

1416
48:04.910 --> 48:09.480
♫One day, we'll find what we're yearning for♫

1417
48:09.500 --> 48:13.010
♫Walking alone is fine, but it's better when you're by my side♫

1418
48:13.030 --> 48:16.610
♫It won't be lonely when you're here to walk beside♫

1419
48:16.630 --> 48:20.150
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

1420
48:20.170 --> 48:22.520
♫Like a love that remains, remains at the dorm♫

1421
48:22.550 --> 48:28.870
♫Meaningful love and good things await on every path♫

1422
48:29.530 --> 48:36.260
♫It might not be a coincidence that we get to meet♫

1423
48:36.740 --> 48:43.890
♫There might be hidden meanings on the path beneath our feet♫

1424
48:43.910 --> 48:46.830
♫Perhaps the D Dorm is what led me to meet you♫
